    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-09-10T21:19:59+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-10T21:19:59+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-10T11:49:59Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-10T11:49:59Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred south of the Bight extends a ridge across the south of SA. The main high centre will gradually move eastwards to be centred to the east of SA on Friday. A trough over the interior of WA will remain stationary but will weaken later Friday. Another low pressure trough will approach from the west on Saturday and move across SA on Sunday then a cold front will move across southern coasts later Monday. An upper disturbance will move over the far west on Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-09-10T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-11T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-10T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-10T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly clear. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Winds easterly 15 to 25 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-09-11T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-12T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-10T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-11T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, most likely in the morning. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy in the morning. Winds east to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 7 and 12 with daytime temperatures reaching the low to mid 20s.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:20am to 3:30pm, UV Index predicted to reach 8 [Very High]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-09-12T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-11T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds in the far west in the evening. Winds northeasterly 15 to 20 km/h tending northwest to northeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 13 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-09-13T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-14T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-12T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-13T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. The chance of a thunderstorm. Winds north to northwesterly 15 to 25 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly 20 to 30 km/h during the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to between 14 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 27 to 34.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-09-14T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-09-15T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-09-13T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-09-14T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Woomera. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. Light winds becoming southeast to southwesterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 10 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching 25 to 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
